%% Real DDL indexes, not hints. Each one is a query the application actually
%% makes — a ward board reading beds by ward and status, a doctor's day reading
%% appointments by doctor and time, a billing screen reading invoices by patient
%% and status — and on a table with a hundred thousand encounters the difference
%% is not academic. The `unique` ones back the UK columns above, which is what
%% makes the customValidate hooks below cheap to enforce.
%%index Patient(medical_record_number) unique
%%index Patient(last_name, first_name)
%%index Staff(employee_number) unique
%%index Doctor(license_number) unique
